# LF is this repository's canonical line ending, everywhere. `* text=auto
# eol=lf` normalizes every checkout to LF regardless of OS or the local
# `core.autocrlf` setting, so a clone is byte-identical on every machine and
# `prettier --check` (which expects LF) is never fooled by the CRLF that
# Windows checkouts with `core.autocrlf=true` write into the working tree.
#
# LF specifically matters in two places that used to have their own narrow
# rule; this one rule is strictly stronger than both, so they are removed
# here as redundant, not forgotten:
# - tests/core/vault/** and tests/fixtures/vault/** are read by string logic
#   (frontmatter splitting, section/heading regexes with `$` anchors) that
#   assumes bare `\n` newlines (story 005).
# - docs/MODULE-SCHEMA.md is compared byte-exact in
#   tests/core/wiki/module.test.ts against a `\n` TS template literal
#   (story 005).
* text=auto eol=lf

# The repo has tracked binaries (assets/**: .png/.ico; .screenshots/*.png)
# that must never be touched by line-ending normalization, so pin them
# explicitly rather than leaving them to git's content-sniffing heuristics.
*.png -text
*.ico -text
